                                              Fault 3 - Wrong default gateway on PC-FIN

Symptom:

PC-FIN (192.168.30.10) could not reach other subnets. Pinging 192.168.20.10 timed out on all 4 packets. Pinging the gateway it was configured with (192.168.30.99) timed out as well.

What I did to break it:

I changed PC-FIN's default gateway to 192.168.30.99, which is an address nothing in the lab uses.

Commands used to diagnose:

C:\> ipconfig
C:\> ping 192.168.30.99
C:\> ping 192.168.30.1

ipconfig showed the gateway as .99. Pinging .99 failed but pinging .1 (the real sub-interface address) worked, which pointed straight at the gateway setting.

Root cause:

PC-FIN was sending everything for other networks to 192.168.30.99. Nothing owns that address so ARP never got a reply and the traffic never left the VLAN. The IP and mask on the PC were fine, which is why it looked like only a local problem.

Fix:

I changed the default gateway on PC-FIN from 192.168.30.99 to 192.168.30.1. The IP (192.168.30.10) and mask (255.255.255.0) stayed the same.

Verification:

C:\> ping 192.168.30.1

Pinging 192.168.30.1 with 32 bytes of data:
Reply from 192.168.30.1: bytes=32 time<1ms TTL=255
Reply from 192.168.30.1: bytes=32 time<1ms TTL=255
Reply from 192.168.30.1: bytes=32 time<1ms TTL=255
Reply from 192.168.30.1: bytes=32 time<1ms TTL=255

Packets: Sent = 4, Received = 4, Lost = 0 (0% loss)
