                                               Fault 5 - Finance sub-interface shut down on the router

Symptom:

PC-FIN (192.168.30.10) could not reach anything, not even its own gateway. Pinging 192.168.30.1 timed out on all 4 packets.

What I did to break it:

On R1-CORE I shut down the Finance sub-interface.

R1-CORE(config)# interface gigabitEthernet0/0.30
R1-CORE(config-subif)# shutdown

Commands used to diagnose:

Router# show ip interface brief

Gi0/0.30 showed as administratively down and the protocol was down too.

Root cause:

Gi0/0.30 is the gateway for VLAN 30 (192.168.30.0/24). With it shut down nothing was answering at 192.168.30.1, so PC-FIN had no gateway at all. The other sub-interfaces were still up so the other VLANs were fine, which showed me it was only Finance.

Fix:

Router> enable
Router# configure terminal
Router(config)# interface gigabitEthernet0/0.30
Router(config-subif)# no shutdown
Router(config-subif)# end
Router# write memory

Verification:

I pinged the gateway from PC-FIN. The first packet timed out while ARP was resolving and then the rest went through.

C:\> ping 192.168.30.1

Pinging 192.168.30.1 with 32 bytes of data:
Request timed out.
Reply from 192.168.30.1: bytes=32 time=4ms TTL=255
Reply from 192.168.30.1: bytes=32 time<1ms TTL=255
Reply from 192.168.30.1: bytes=32 time<1ms TTL=255

Packets: Sent = 4, Received = 3, Lost = 1 (25% loss)
